<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Hungarian State (1849)</h1><p class="st-meta">1849 CE – 1849 CE · capital Debrecen</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Independent Hungary proclaimed in Debrecen during the revolution of 1848 to 1849, which dethroned the Habsburgs and was crushed by Austrian and Russian armies.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary's</a> revolution of 1848 began with the April Laws, but by winter the court in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> was at war with the Hungarian government. After the spring campaign drove back Austrian forces, the Hungarian parliament, meeting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/debrecen">Debrecen</a>, adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-declaration-of-independence">Declaration of Independence</a> on 14 April 1849, deposing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg dynasty</a> and electing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lajos-kossuth">Lajos Kossuth</a> governor-president.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The new state left the question of monarchy or republic undecided. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lajos-kossuth">Kossuth</a> headed the state, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bertalan-szemere">Bertalan Szemere's</a> government ran affairs, and the honvéd army under commanders such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artur-gorgei">Artúr Görgei</a> recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buda">Buda</a> in May 1849. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paper-money">Paper money</a>, the Kossuth notes, financed the war. Relations with Romanian, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serb</a> and Croat minorities stayed hostile until a late nationalities law in July.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Russian intervention in June 1849 tipped the balance, and Görgei surrendered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surrender-at-vilagos">Világos</a> on 13 August. Thirteen generals were executed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arad-romania">Arad</a> in October, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lajos-kossuth">Kossuth</a> went into exile. Neo-absolutist rule followed until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Compromise of 1867</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/hungarian-state-1849.jpg" alt="Hungarian State (1849)" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hungary_with_great_coat_of_arms_(1849).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1849 CE – 1849 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Debrecen</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lajos Kossuth, Bertalan Szemere, Artúr Görgei</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic and Protestant Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hungarian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a href="/countries/slovakia">Slovakia</a>, <a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hungarian Revolutionary State, Hungarian State of 1849</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1849&amp;focus=hungarian-state-1849" aria-label="Hungarian State (1849) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5186 511 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hungarian State (1849) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5506 767L5381 747"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5506 767h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5506 767h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Debrecen. <a href="/atlas?year=1849&amp;focus=hungarian-state-1849">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
